// APW-5 — Event ordering (A must precede B) — BUGGY variant.
//
// Same intent as the correct variant (read-before-write), but the events are
// `response` instead of `request`. The ordering is then enforced only on
// *settled* events, so a `Write` can be admitted before the corresponding
// `Read` has settled — an out-of-order write (the ordering hole).
//
// The one-word bug vs. the correct variant: `response` instead of `request`.
//
// Schema: Drupe namespace.
// See: rot/shapes.py (build_event_ordering_ir -- the hand-written oracle).
@id("event_ordering_buggy")
forbid (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Write",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h (
        Drupe::Action::"Read"::response{ input.key: context.input.key }
        && Drupe::Action::"Write"::response{ input.key: context.input.key }
    )
};